  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-134089\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>Let's examine the given situation.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>The <em>positive</em> linear correlation means that the data points should be scattered along a line with a <em>positive</em> slope. </p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Since the correlation is <em>weak</em>, most of the points should be scattered <em>far</em> from the trend line.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, this situation corresponds to the following scatter plot.</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-134089-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-134089-e-0\"></div> <div class=\"studentAnswerHeader\">Your Answer:</div><div class=\"studentAnswer\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-134089-a-3\">   </div></div>",
